1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,812
You get a Java project. You type M V N package. And it builds. What just happened?

2
00:00:06,362 --> 00:00:07,646
Maven read one file,

3
00:00:07,646 --> 00:00:08,160
the pom.

4
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:09,765
It knew the project name,

5
00:00:09,765 --> 00:00:10,536
the folders,

6
00:00:10,536 --> 00:00:11,435
the libraries,

7
00:00:11,435 --> 00:00:12,719
and the build steps.

8
00:00:13,269 --> 00:00:15,367
Today you learn to read that file,

9
00:00:15,367 --> 00:00:17,342
the folder layout Maven expects,

10
00:00:17,342 --> 00:00:19,008
and how it finds a library.

11
00:00:19,558 --> 00:00:21,755
Then you fix a broken project yourself.

12
00:00:22,305 --> 00:00:23,364
One honest note.

13
00:00:23,364 --> 00:00:26,605
My recording computer cannot reach Maven Central,

14
00:00:26,605 --> 00:00:29,846
so these demos use a local copy of the libraries.

15
00:00:29,846 --> 00:00:32,823
The commands are the same ones you will type.

16
00:00:34,373 --> 00:00:37,850
A pom is an X M L file. Four parts matter first.

17
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:38,710
One.

18
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:39,639
Coordinates.

19
00:00:39,639 --> 00:00:40,413
Group I D,

20
00:00:40,413 --> 00:00:41,420
artifact I D,

21
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:42,349
and version.

22
00:00:42,349 --> 00:00:43,046
Together,

23
00:00:43,046 --> 00:00:43,510
G A V.

24
00:00:43,510 --> 00:00:45,291
They name your project,

25
00:00:45,291 --> 00:00:46,685
and every library,

26
00:00:46,685 --> 00:00:47,382
uniquely.

27
00:00:47,932 --> 00:00:51,537
Two. Properties. Settings like the Java release, written once.

28
00:00:52,087 --> 00:00:52,467
Three.

29
00:00:52,467 --> 00:00:53,290
Dependencies.

30
00:00:53,290 --> 00:00:54,747
The libraries you need.

31
00:00:54,747 --> 00:00:57,343
Each one is named by its own coordinates,

32
00:00:57,343 --> 00:00:58,103
and a scope.

33
00:00:58,653 --> 00:01:03,389
Four. Build. The plugins that compile, test and package, with their versions pinned.

34
00:01:03,939 --> 00:01:04,820
And one rule.

35
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:06,854
Convention over configuration.

36
00:01:06,854 --> 00:01:09,226
Put files where Maven expects them,

37
00:01:09,226 --> 00:01:11,192
and you write almost nothing.

38
00:01:13,242 --> 00:01:15,104
Where do libraries live?

39
00:01:15,104 --> 00:01:16,345
In a repository.

40
00:01:16,345 --> 00:01:18,595
A repository is only folders,

41
00:01:18,595 --> 00:01:20,457
shown here over H T T P.

42
00:01:20,457 --> 00:01:22,086
This is a local copy,

43
00:01:22,086 --> 00:01:23,482
not Maven Central.

44
00:01:24,032 --> 00:01:28,064
The group I D, org dot apache dot commons, becomes folders.

45
00:01:33,114 --> 00:01:35,887
Next, the artifact I D, commons lang three.

46
00:01:36,437 --> 00:01:39,083
Then the version, three point fourteen point zero.

47
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:41,012
Inside: the jar,

48
00:01:41,012 --> 00:01:41,552
the pom,

49
00:01:41,552 --> 00:01:42,834
and checksum files.

50
00:01:42,834 --> 00:01:44,859
Every library has its own pom,

51
00:01:44,859 --> 00:01:46,546
with its own coordinates.

52
00:01:49,996 --> 00:01:54,433
Maven Central uses this exact layout. Same folders, same names.

53
00:01:56,383 --> 00:01:59,540
Go to the demo project. Type: CD, demo.

54
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:04,912
Read the top of the pom. Type: head -16 pom.xml

55
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:06,174
The coordinates.

56
00:02:06,174 --> 00:02:07,518
Com dot cloud cart,

57
00:02:07,518 --> 00:02:08,438
greeter demo,

58
00:02:08,438 --> 00:02:10,278
one point zero point zero.

59
00:02:10,278 --> 00:02:12,188
That is the project's name.

60
00:02:12,738 --> 00:02:17,496
Maven expects standard folders. Type: find src -type f

61
00:02:17,626 --> 00:02:22,042
Main code under source, main, java. Tests under source, test, java.

62
00:02:22,592 --> 00:02:27,306
Which Maven is this? Type: mvn -v | head -1

63
00:02:27,436 --> 00:02:29,506
Maven three point nine point eleven.

64
00:02:30,056 --> 00:02:36,114
Build it. Type: mvn -B -q package 2>&1 | head -3

65
00:02:36,244 --> 00:02:36,883
It fails.

66
00:02:36,883 --> 00:02:41,782
The package org dot apache dot commons dot lang three does not exist.

67
00:02:41,782 --> 00:02:45,332
The code imports a library the pom never declared.

68
00:02:47,382 --> 00:02:50,539
Go to the demo project. Type: CD, demo.

69
00:02:51,089 --> 00:02:56,359
Where is the library used? Type: grep import src/main/java/cloudcart/Hello.java

70
00:02:56,489 --> 00:03:00,905
It imports string utils from commons lang three. So the pom must declare it.

71
00:03:01,455 --> 00:03:05,337
Here is the block to add. Type: cat dep.xml

72
00:03:05,467 --> 00:03:10,694
Group I D, artifact I D, version. Three coordinates. That is a dependency.

73
00:03:11,244 --> 00:03:19,159
Insert it into the pom. Type: sed -i '/<dependencies>/r dep.xml' pom.xml

74
00:03:19,289 --> 00:03:25,155
Build again. Type: mvn -B package | grep -E 'Tests run:|BUILD'

75
00:03:25,285 --> 00:03:26,427
While Maven works,

76
00:03:26,427 --> 00:03:27,758
it compiles the code,

77
00:03:27,758 --> 00:03:29,471
compiles and runs the test,

78
00:03:29,471 --> 00:03:30,612
and packs the jar.

79
00:03:30,612 --> 00:03:32,197
That takes a few seconds.

80
00:03:35,247 --> 00:03:37,999
One test ran, none failed. Build success.

81
00:03:38,549 --> 00:03:42,581
What did it make? Type: ls target/*.jar

82
00:03:42,711 --> 00:03:47,341
The jar is named from the coordinates. Artifact I D, dash, version.

83
00:03:47,891 --> 00:03:54,803
See the dependency tree. Type: mvn -B dependency:tree | grep 'jar:'

84
00:03:55,433 --> 00:03:56,264
Our project.

85
00:03:56,264 --> 00:03:58,202
One library to compile with.

86
00:03:58,202 --> 00:03:58,687
J unit,

87
00:03:58,687 --> 00:03:59,725
for tests only,

88
00:03:59,725 --> 00:04:01,110
with its own helper.

89
00:04:01,110 --> 00:04:03,049
Test scope is never shipped.

90
00:04:03,599 --> 00:04:11,428
Where did that jar come from? Type: find ~/.m2 -name 'commons-lang3-3*.jar'

91
00:04:11,558 --> 00:04:13,652
Cached in your local repository,

92
00:04:13,652 --> 00:04:16,204
under the same folders we just browsed.

93
00:04:16,204 --> 00:04:18,363
The next build needs no download.

94
00:04:20,413 --> 00:04:22,973
How Maven finds a library, in this order.

95
00:04:23,523 --> 00:04:23,937
First,

96
00:04:23,937 --> 00:04:25,456
your local repository,

97
00:04:25,456 --> 00:04:27,804
the dot M two folder in your home.

98
00:04:27,804 --> 00:04:29,185
If the jar is there,

99
00:04:29,185 --> 00:04:29,944
it is used.

100
00:04:30,494 --> 00:04:31,029
If not,

101
00:04:31,029 --> 00:04:32,556
a remote repository.

102
00:04:32,556 --> 00:04:33,396
By default,

103
00:04:33,396 --> 00:04:34,465
Maven Central.

104
00:04:34,465 --> 00:04:35,916
Maven downloads it,

105
00:04:35,916 --> 00:04:37,214
and keeps a copy.

106
00:04:37,764 --> 00:04:42,799
The path comes from the coordinates. Same coordinates, same file, on any computer.

107
00:04:43,349 --> 00:04:46,314
So pin your versions. Same version, same build.

108
00:04:48,364 --> 00:04:49,232
Your lab task.

109
00:04:49,232 --> 00:04:52,705
Lab eighty-five gives you a project that will not build.

110
00:04:52,705 --> 00:04:54,380
Lab check judges your work.

111
00:04:54,930 --> 00:04:57,075
It lives at git hub dot com,

112
00:04:57,075 --> 00:04:58,607
slash it dash waves,

113
00:04:58,607 --> 00:05:00,369
slash dev ops dash A I,

114
00:05:00,369 --> 00:05:01,212
in academy,

115
00:05:01,212 --> 00:05:01,518
lab,

116
00:05:01,518 --> 00:05:03,357
lab eighty-five dot S H.

117
00:05:03,907 --> 00:05:10,072
One: set the coordinates. Com dot cloud cart, cart API, one point zero point zero.

118
00:05:10,622 --> 00:05:15,891
Two: move the source into source, main, java, and the test into source, test, java.

119
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:18,564
Three: declare commons lang three,

120
00:05:18,564 --> 00:05:20,562
three point fourteen point zero,

121
00:05:20,562 --> 00:05:21,249
and J unit,

122
00:05:21,249 --> 00:05:23,122
four point thirteen point two,

123
00:05:23,122 --> 00:05:24,121
with scope test.

124
00:05:24,671 --> 00:05:30,367
Four: M V N package. It must end in build success, and make the cart API jar.

125
00:05:30,917 --> 00:05:34,181
Five: save the dependency tree into tree dot text.

126
00:05:34,731 --> 00:05:37,090
Install a J D K and Maven first.

127
00:05:37,090 --> 00:05:37,974
Then lab up,

128
00:05:37,974 --> 00:05:38,711
lab check,

129
00:05:38,711 --> 00:05:39,669
and lab down.

130
00:05:39,669 --> 00:05:42,838
The shortcut file is shortcuts eighty-five.

131
00:05:44,888 --> 00:05:46,957
Pass or fail. You need all six.

132
00:05:47,507 --> 00:05:49,321
Five pass lines in lab check.

133
00:05:49,871 --> 00:05:51,641
You can name the three coordinates.

134
00:05:52,191 --> 00:05:54,090
You can explain the standard folders.

135
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:57,051
You can explain compile scope and test scope.

136
00:05:57,601 --> 00:05:59,990
You can say where Maven caches a library.

137
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:02,460
lab down, nothing left behind.

138
00:06:03,010 --> 00:06:04,311
To pass, all six.

139
00:06:06,361 --> 00:06:09,198
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

140
00:06:09,748 --> 00:06:11,839
One: lab up, and read the task file.

141
00:06:12,389 --> 00:06:15,610
Two: run M V N package, and read the first error.

142
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:18,550
Three: fix the coordinates and the folders.

143
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:21,105
Four: declare the two dependencies.

144
00:06:21,655 --> 00:06:24,599
Five: build, save tree dot text, and lab check.

145
00:06:25,149 --> 00:06:27,730
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

146
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,115
Pause the video, and begin now.

147
00:06:45,665 --> 00:06:46,540
Quick check.

148
00:06:47,090 --> 00:06:49,074
Which three values are the coordinates?

149
00:06:49,624 --> 00:06:51,053
Where must main code live?

150
00:06:51,603 --> 00:06:53,075
Which scope is not shipped?

151
00:06:53,625 --> 00:06:56,292
Where does Maven keep a downloaded library?

152
00:06:56,842 --> 00:07:00,063
Objective covered: M C ten, objective one.

153
00:07:00,613 --> 00:07:02,682
